      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the probability that a randomly selected card from a box of 50 cards (numbered from 1 to 50) has a prime number that is also a multiple of 7, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the prime numbers that are multiples of 7:**\n   A prime number is a number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself. The only prime number that is a multiple of 7 is 7 itself. This is because any number that is a multiple of 7 and is also a prime number would have to be a multiple of 7 and its only divisors would be 1 and 7, which contradicts the definition of a prime number.\n\n2. **Determine the total number of favorable outcomes:**\n   The only prime number that is a multiple of 7 is 7. Therefore, there is only 1 favorable outcome.\n\n3. **Determine the total number of possible outcomes:**\n   There are 50 possible outcomes since there are 50 cards in the box.\n\n4. **Calculate the probability:**\n   The probability \\( P \\) of selecting a card with a prime number that is a multiple of 7 is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes. So,\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of possible outcomes}} = \\frac{1}{50}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that the number on the card is prime and is a multiple of 7 is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{50}}\\).",
